{"id":"H7817","lemma":"שָׁחַח","transliteration":"shachach","sayIt":"sha-chach","language":"Hebrew","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to bow","meaning":"1) to bow, crouch, bow down, be bowed down\n1a) (Qal)\n1a1) to be bowed down, be prostrated, be humbled\n1a2) to bow (in homage)\n1a3) to bow (of mourner)\n1a4) to crouch (of wild beast in lair)\n1b) (Niphal) to be prostrated, be humbled, be reduced, be weakened, proceed humbly, be bowed down\n1c) (Hiphil) to prostrate, lay low, bow down\n1d) (Hithpolel) to be cast down, be despairing","glosses":["brought low","downcast","cower","crouch","beaten down","bowed down with"],"count":21,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"job-9","v":13,"renderings":{"bsb":"cower"}},{"chapterId":"job-38","v":40,"renderings":{"bsb":"they crouch","kjv":"When they couch"}},{"chapterId":"psa-10","v":10,"renderings":{"bsb":"and beaten down","kjv":"and humbleth"}},{"chapterId":"psa-35","v":14,"renderings":{"bsb":"was bowed down with","kjv":"I bowed down"}},{"chapterId":"psa-38","v":6,"renderings":{"bsb":"and brought low","kjv":"I am bowed down"}},{"chapterId":"psa-42","v":5,"renderings":{"bsb":"are you downcast","kjv":"Why art thou cast down"}},{"chapterId":"psa-42","v":6,"renderings":{"bsb":"despairs","kjv":"is cast down"}},{"chapterId":"psa-42","v":11,"renderings":{"bsb":"are you downcast","kjv":"Why art thou cast down"}},{"chapterId":"psa-43","v":5,"renderings":{"bsb":"are you downcast","kjv":"Why art thou cast down"}},{"chapterId":"psa-107","v":39,"renderings":{"bsb":"and humbled","kjv":"and brought low"}},{"chapterId":"pro-14","v":19,"renderings":{"bsb":"bow","kjv":"bow"}},{"chapterId":"ecc-12","v":4,"renderings":{"bsb":"grow faint"}},{"chapterId":"isa-2","v":9,"renderings":{"bsb":"is brought low","kjv":"boweth down"}},{"chapterId":"isa-2","v":11,"renderings":{"bsb":"brought low","kjv":"shall be bowed down"}},{"chapterId":"isa-2","v":17,"renderings":{"bsb":"will be brought low","kjv":"shall be bowed down"}},{"chapterId":"isa-5","v":15,"renderings":{"bsb":"will be brought low","kjv":"shall be brought down"}},{"chapterId":"isa-25","v":12,"renderings":{"bsb":"will be brought down","kjv":"shall he bring down"}},{"chapterId":"isa-26","v":5,"renderings":{"bsb":"He has humbled","kjv":"For he bringeth down"}},{"chapterId":"isa-29","v":4,"renderings":{"bsb":"will be muffled","kjv":"shall be low"}},{"chapterId":"isa-60","v":14,"renderings":{"bsb":"and bow down","kjv":"bending"}},{"chapterId":"hab-3","v":6,"renderings":{"bsb":"collapsed","kjv":"did bow"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Job 9:13","note":"“God will not withdraw his anger. The helpers of Rahab stoop under him.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Psalm 10:10","note":"The helpless are crushed. They collapse. They fall under his strength.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Proverbs 14:19","note":"The evil bow down before the good, and the wicked at the gates of the righteous.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Ecclesiastes 12:4","note":"and the doors shall be shut in the street; when the sound of the grinding is low, and one shall rise up at the voice of a bird, and all the daughters of music…","source":"web"},{"ref":"Isaiah 2:9","note":"Man is brought low, and mankind is humbled; therefore don’t forgive them.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Habakkuk 3:6","note":"He stood, and shook the earth. He looked, and made the nations tremble. The ancient mountains were crumbled. The age-old hills collapsed. His ways are eternal.","source":"web"}],"related":[],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}